WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.408 --> 00:00:02.991
(bright music)

00:00:05.537 --> 00:00:07.875
- [Narrator] During the
annual crab migration,

00:00:07.875 --> 00:00:11.042
all of Christmas Island is seeing red.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:16.587
Christmas Island, located
in the Pacific Ocean

00:00:16.587 --> 00:00:21.058
near Australia, is known for
its warm tropical climate.

00:00:21.058 --> 00:00:22.807
Throughout most of the year,

00:00:22.807 --> 00:00:26.957
its endemic red crabs can be
found on the rainforest floor.

00:00:26.957 --> 00:00:28.909
But each year in late October,

00:00:28.909 --> 00:00:32.376
the adult crabs begin a
spectacular mass migration

00:00:32.376 --> 00:00:34.573
from the rainforest to the coast

00:00:34.573 --> 00:00:37.901
to breed and release eggs into the sea.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:42.178
This synchronized breeding
of about 40 million crabs

00:00:42.178 --> 00:00:44.504
takes over the tiny island.

00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:46.691
They take their cues
from a unique combination

00:00:46.691 --> 00:00:49.613
of weather and the movement of the moon.

00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:52.524
As the rains of the
monsoon wet season return,

00:00:52.524 --> 00:00:54.696
they begin their journey.

00:00:54.696 --> 00:00:56.904
The crabs arrive at the coast,

00:00:56.904 --> 00:01:00.040
where they dig burrows for mating,

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.144
and then the females release
their eggs into the sea,

00:01:03.144 --> 00:01:07.709
just as the high tide from
the new moon hits the shore.

00:01:07.709 --> 00:01:11.709
These crabs are so reliant
on these seasonal cues

00:01:11.709 --> 00:01:14.611
that if the wet season
doesn't arrive on time,

00:01:14.611 --> 00:01:18.899
the crabs will not spawn
until the next lunar month.

00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:21.000
They make their migrations
without much care

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.366
for road rules or streets,

00:01:23.366 --> 00:01:26.611
which results in incredible
and slightly startling waves

00:01:26.611 --> 00:01:29.778
of red crabs moving across the island.

